# The sidecar is a separate image, built from ./enquiry with its own
# Dockerfile. The site build copied this directory in and never used it.
#
# An earlier version of this comment blamed the .woff2 files under
# enquiry/fonts for the Turbopack font failures in CI. That was wrong. The
# same content passed on a branch and failed on main minutes later, and the
# real cause was next/font/google fetching from the network during the build
# — see src/app/layout.tsx, which no longer does. Keeping the directory out
# of a context that has no use for it is still right; it just never fixed
# anything.
enquiry/

# Reference capture — hundreds of MB, not needed to build
capture/
design/
docs/
deliverables/
brand/*.png

*.md
!README.md
.DS_Store

# Image derivatives live in GCS behind the CDN, not in the container. The
# build only needs src/generated/images.json — it reads dimensions, LQIPs and
# the derivative paths from the manifest and emits absolute CDN URLs, so
# shipping the files too would add ~165 MB to every push and node pull for
# bytes nginx would never serve.
#
# Keep public/brand: the logo SVGs are tiny and are referenced same-origin.
public/img/
